From 6a1e02d96ca6e3750e4290476cf1fe5741c46d3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 21:48:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] trebledroid-staging: gate fake hw-keyboard skip on xiaomi
 pad6 (pipa)

xiaomi pad6 (pipa) ships vendor.xiaomi.hardware.keyboardnanoapp, a CHRE
nanoapp driven by a hall sensor, that registers two alphabetic
(KEYBOARD_TYPE_ALPHABETIC) input devices even when the magnetic keyboard
cover is detached. DisplayContent.computeConfiguration treats any
alphabetic input device as a real hardware keyboard and sets
Configuration.keyboard=KEYBOARD_QWERTY with hardKeyboardHidden=NO for
every app.

that configuration makes soft IMEs suppress their key views: LatinIME's
KeyboardSwitcher.setMainKeyboardFrame hides mKeyboardView based only on
mHasHardwareKeyboard && toggleState==HIDDEN and does not consult
Settings.Secure.SHOW_IME_WITH_HARD_KEYBOARD, so the trebledroid toggle
only makes the framework show the IME window while the IME itself blanks
the keys. user-installed IMEs (e.g. Fossify) hit the same path and cannot
be patched from the GSI tree.

set persist.sys.phh.disable_fake_hw_keyboard on pipa so the
DisplayContent patch can skip the nanoapp keyboards and keep
Configuration.keyboard=KEYBOARD_NOKEYS, restoring soft input for all
IMEs.
---
 rw-system.sh | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rw-system.sh b/rw-system.sh
index 71fb905..3ab5e42 100644
--- a/rw-system.sh
+++ b/rw-system.sh
@@ -202,6 +202,14 @@ changeKeylayout() {
         changed=true
     fi
 
+    # xiaomi pad6 (pipa) ships a CHRE keyboardnanoapp + hall sensor that register
+    # two alphabetic input devices even with the keyboard cover detached, which
+    # forces Configuration.keyboard=QWERTY and makes soft IMEs hide their keys.
+    # gate the DisplayContent workaround behind this property.
+    if getprop ro.vendor.build.fingerprint | grep -iq -e xiaomi/pipa; then
+        setprop persist.sys.phh.disable_fake_hw_keyboard true
+    fi
+
     if getprop ro.vendor.build.fingerprint |grep -iq -e samsung/a10sxx;then
         mkdir -p /data/vendor/mcRegistry
         chown system /data/vendor/mcRegistry
